exports[`git.commit.sponsor.sh given: [case4] the ACTOR guard — a clone cannot bind or clear when: [t0] set with no tty on any stream then: refuses, and names the channel as the cause 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.commit.sponsor set
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: no terminal on this command

   only a human at a real terminal may bind or clear a sponsor, and
   this command has none. a clone's tool call has none, and neither
   does a claude \`!\` command, so the two cannot be told apart here.

   if you are a clone: this holds even for a real human's name. to
   name a human who did not act is a fabrication, and it reads as
   authorized. hand this to your human.

run it from your own terminal, in this tree:
  $ printf 'Name <email>' | rhx git.commit.sponsor set --who @stdin
  $ rhx git.commit.sponsor set --who "Name <email>"
"
`;

exports[`git.commit.sponsor.sh given: [case4] the ACTOR guard — a clone cannot bind or clear when: [t1] del with no tty then: refuses too, and leaves the sponsor bound 1`] = `
